    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1337">

                <pb facs="1595" n="1397" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24591/7–3045: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1337<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-30T13:00:00+03:25">July 30, 1945—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>560. Booth has received further telegram<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1337-f1"/> from
                    Potsdam canceling War telegram reported mytel 554 July 28<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1337-f2"/> and authorizing more gradual withdrawal troops from
                    Iran. He is now instructed transfer HQ (headquarters) from Amirabad to
                    Khorramshahr by October 1 but to leave custodial detachment at Amirabad. Orders
                    state OANLC (Office Army Navy Liquidation Commissioner]) staff will remain
                    here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Murray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
